</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Consistency with Human Judgment</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To comprehensively evaluate end-to-end speech LLMs, we computed the Pearson correlation coefficients between the evaluation methods of WildSpeech, VoiceBench<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
              
              
              
            Voicebench contains several subsets and we use prompts from its open-ended QA sets for a fair comparison.</span></span></span>, and human expert evaluation, as shown in Figure <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 Experimental Results ‣ WildSpeech-Bench: Benchmarking Audio LLMs in Natural Speech Conversation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. The experimental results reveal that WildSpeech’s evaluation method exhibits a significantly higher correlation coefficient with human expert evaluation than VoiceBench. This finding indicates that WildSpeech’s evaluation approach aligns more closely with human auditory perception, providing a more reliable assessment of model performance in real-world scenarios.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Moreover, we further explored the impact of two key factors in WildSpeech’s evaluation process: query-aware evaluation and multi-round ASR + evaluation. By comparing the correlation coefficients across six distinct scenarios, we aimed to comprehensively assess the contributions of these factors to model evaluation accuracy and reliability.
In scenarios <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 Experimental Results ‣ WildSpeech-Bench: Benchmarking Audio LLMs in Natural Speech Conversation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>-<a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 Experimental Results ‣ WildSpeech-Bench: Benchmarking Audio LLMs in Natural Speech Conversation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we systematically varied the presence and number of ASR + evaluation rounds, as well as query-aware evaluation:
(1) Our automatic evaluation (featuring three rounds of ASR + evaluation and query-aware evaluation), corresponding to Figure <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 Experimental Results ‣ WildSpeech-Bench: Benchmarking Audio LLMs in Natural Speech Conversation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
(2) Our evaluation without query-aware evaluation, corresponding to Figure <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 Experimental Results ‣ WildSpeech-Bench: Benchmarking Audio LLMs in Natural Speech Conversation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
(3) VoiceBench’s evaluation, corresponding to Figure <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 Experimental Results ‣ WildSpeech-Bench: Benchmarking Audio LLMs in Natural Speech Conversation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
(4) Our evaluation with only one round of ASR + evaluation, corresponding to Figure <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 Experimental Results ‣ WildSpeech-Bench: Benchmarking Audio LLMs in Natural Speech Conversation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The results from these comparisons clearly demonstrate that both multi-round ASR + evaluation and query-aware evaluation play crucial roles in enhancing the correlation between automatic and human expert evaluations. Multiple rounds of ASR and evaluation, together with query-aware evaluation, significantly reduce evaluation errors and improve consistency with human judgment.
To further isolate and validate the impact of query-aware evaluation, we analyzed two additional scenarios on a carefully selected subset of data:
(1) Evaluation on a subset of data with query-aware evaluation applied (Figure <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 Experimental Results ‣ WildSpeech-Bench: Benchmarking Audio LLMs in Natural Speech Conversation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>);
(2) Evaluation on the same subset of data before applying query-aware evaluation (Figure <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 Experimental Results ‣ WildSpeech-Bench: Benchmarking Audio LLMs in Natural Speech Conversation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).
Since not all queries in the dataset are suitable for query-aware evaluation, this subset was chosen to highlight the specific benefits of this evaluation method. The results provide evidence that query-aware evaluation is a key factor in enhancing the accuracy and reliability of model evaluation. By focusing on relevant aspects of each query, this approach effectively captures the nuances of model performance, leading to more precise and meaningful evaluation results.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F6.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:165.6pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.21875v1/noise_graph.svg" id="S4.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:229/137;" width="229" height="137"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F6.fig1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="S4.F6.fig1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Influence of noise on response quality.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
