<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Evaluation Prompt</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="824.28" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 824.28" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,824.28) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#6B0061;" fill="#6B0061" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 9.84 L 0 814.43 C 0 819.87 4.41 824.28 9.84 824.28 L 467.53 824.28 C 472.97 824.28 477.38 819.87 477.38 814.43 L 477.38 9.84 C 477.38 4.41 472.97 0 467.53 0 L 9.84 0 C 4.41 0 0 4.41 0 9.84 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 9.84 L 1.97 783.56 L 475.41 783.56 L 475.41 9.84 C 475.41 5.49 471.88 1.97 467.53 1.97 L 9.84 1.97 C 5.49 1.97 1.97 5.49 1.97 9.84 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 792.16)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:27.28em;--ltx-fo-height:1.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="28.9" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 26.21)" width="377.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:27.28em;">
<span id="A3.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block fa fa-info-circle" aria-hidden="true">
</span>
<span id="A3.p1.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Evaluation Prompt</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.89)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.91em;--ltx-fo-height:54.55em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.23em;font-size:10pt;" height="757.98" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 754.87)" width="469.22"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.91em;">
<span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"># Instructions

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">You are an evaluation expert. Your task is to assess the quality of AI model responses. We will provide you with user queries and AI responses. Please note that both the user queries and AI responses are in audio format. For your convenience, we have converted them into text, but you should evaluate from the perspective of voice communication and analyze the characteristics of voice communication when assessing the quality of the AI response.

<br class="ltx_break">You should first carefully read the user query to analyze the task, then evaluate the quality of the response based on the rules provided below.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"># Conversation between User and AI

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">### User Query</span></span><pre id="A3.p1.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">

&lt;|begin_of_query|&gt;

{query}

&lt;|end_of_query|&gt;

</pre>
<span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">### AI Response</span></span><pre id="A3.p1.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
&lt;|begin_of_response|&gt;

{response}

&lt;|end_of_response|&gt;


</pre>
<span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"># Evaluation

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">## Checklist

<br class="ltx_break"></span></span><pre id="A3.p1.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
&lt;|begin_of_checklist|&gt;

{checklist}

&lt;|end_of_checklist|&gt;


</pre>
<span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The checklist serves as a guiding framework for your evaluation. However, feel free to consider aspects beyond its contents to ensure a well - rounded assessment.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">## Rules

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">You should evaluate based on the analysis of user questions and AI responses, referring to the contents in the checklist during the evaluation. However, remember that the checklist is meant to provide comprehensive reference information, but it is not the standard answer. Sometimes, the AI response does not need to cover all the contents involved in the checklist to meet user needs, and you need to make this judgment on your own. The scoring scale ranges from 1 to 10:</span></span>
<span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- 1~2 points: No value/meaningless. The AI response contains many factual errors or serious flaws, or is irrelevant to the user query, providing little to no value to the user.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- 3~4 points: Partially valuable/meaningful. The AI response contains several factual errors or serious flaws, or poorly meets the user’s requirements, but has some redeeming qualities and offers partial value to the user.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- 5~6 points: Flawed. The AI response has some issues, such as minor factual errors/flaws, or does not fully meet the user’s requirements. However, these are relatively minor, and the response generally satisfies the user’s needs.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- 7~8 points: Meets requirements. The AI response satisfies the user’s needs well, with no major flaws or errors, or only very minor issues that do not affect overall quality.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- 9~10 points: High quality. The AI response perfectly meets the user’s requirements, with virtually no room for improvement.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">## Output Format

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">First, analyze the query itself and understand the user’s intent. Then provide your analysis of the model’s response. Summarize your evaluation in two aspects: "Strengths" and "Weaknesses". Finally, write your score. The score should appear on the last line in the following format:
Score: [your score]</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Broader impacts</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our work yields far-positive social impacts, but also necessitates careful consideration of potential societal implications.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">On the positive front, by developing comprehensive test sets for end-to-end speech large models, we enhance the reliability and accuracy of speech technologies. These advancements benefit diverse applications, including virtual assistants, accessibility tools for the visually and hearing impaired, and language learning platforms, thereby fostering inclusivity and equitable information access. Moreover, more robust evaluation mechanisms can steer the development of speech AI towards ethical and responsible trajectories, mitigating potential biases and ensuring these technologies serve the public interest. Our contributions may also accelerate the adoption of speech large models across healthcare, customer service, and education sectors, driving innovation and improving the overall quality of life.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">However, as we strive to elevate the assessment paradigm of end-to-end speech large language models (LLMs), we must acknowledge the potential societal ramifications. The proposed benchmarking framework could inadvertently exacerbate pre-existing biases in the training corpus. Specifically, skewed linguistic distributions across dialectal variations, prosodic patterns, or demographic strata within the test set may propagate evaluative inequities, creating systemic disadvantages for marginalized communities. For example, models may exhibit misattributed performance decrements when processing speech from underrepresented groups, potentially hindering technological adoption and impeding the advancement of speech processing capabilities in these contexts.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Limitations</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our work has two primary limitations. First, although we have made extensive efforts to simulate real-world speech scenarios by carefully designing the query distribution and incorporating various types of noise, the lack of actual in-the-wild speech data for comparison may still lead to discrepancies between our simulated data and real-world situations. Second, multi-turn interactions are a crucial form of communication in speech scenarios, enabling complex capabilities such as context understanding, topic continuation, and intent tracking. However, our current benchmark focuses solely on single-turn dialogue evaluation, failing to comprehensively capture the intricacies of multi-turn speech interactions. As a result, the evaluation of models’ comprehensive capabilities in realistic dialogue scenarios remains incomplete. To address these limitations, expanding the dataset to cover multi-turn interactions more thoroughly will be a key direction for future research.</p>
</div>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
